// Title: VBA DLL Loaded Via Office Application
// ID: e6ce8457-68b1-485b-9bdd-3c2b5d679aa9
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Antonlovesdnb
// Date: 2020-02-19
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1204.002
// Description: Detects VB DLL's loaded by an office application. Which could indicate the presence of VBA Macros.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((Image ENDSWITH "\\excel.exe" OR Image ENDSWITH "\\mspub.exe" OR Image ENDSWITH "\\onenote.exe" OR Image ENDSWITH "\\onenoteim.exe" OR Image ENDSWITH "\\outlook.exe" OR Image ENDSWITH "\\powerpnt.exe" OR Image ENDSWITH "\\winword.exe") AND (ImageLoaded ENDSWITH "\\VBE7.DLL" OR ImageLoaded ENDSWITH "\\VBEUI.DLL" OR ImageLoaded ENDSWITH "\\VBE7INTL.DLL"))
